  "description": "UKANEA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C164 H160 Dy8 N14 O64. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.674-3.853 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.49-109.25°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy8(HL)10(C6H4NH2COO)2(μ3-OH)8(OH)2(NO3)2(H2O)4]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
